@startuml
title Facade - Orquestacion de casos de uso
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class ServiceDeskFacade <<Facade>> {
  -_repository: TicketRepositoryInterface
  -_user_repository: UserRepositoryInterface
  -_subject: TicketSubject
  -_email_notifier: EmailNotifierObserver
  +login(email: str, password: str): TokenResponse
  +get_current_user_from_token(token: str): UserResponse
  +seed_default_users(): List[UserResponse]
  +list_users(role: Optional[str]): List[UserResponse]
  +create_user(request: UserCreateRequest): UserResponse
  +create_ticket(request: TicketCreateRequest): TicketResponse
  +assign_ticket(ticket_id: int, request: TicketAssignRequest): TicketResponse
  +delete_ticket(ticket_id: int): bool
}

interface TicketRepositoryInterface
interface UserRepositoryInterface
class TicketSubject <<Observer Subject>>
class EmailNotifierObserver <<Observer>>
class TicketFactoryRegistry <<Factory Registry>>
class TicketEvent <<Domain Event>>
class TicketModel <<ORM Entity>>
class TicketResponse <<DTO>>

ServiceDeskFacade --> TicketRepositoryInterface : persists tickets and audit logs
ServiceDeskFacade --> UserRepositoryInterface : authenticates and manages users
ServiceDeskFacade --> TicketSubject : dispatches ticket events
ServiceDeskFacade --> EmailNotifierObserver : exposes notification history
ServiceDeskFacade ..> TicketFactoryRegistry : selects category factory
ServiceDeskFacade ..> TicketEvent : publishes
ServiceDeskFacade ..> TicketModel : coordinates domain model
ServiceDeskFacade ..> TicketResponse : returns DTO

note right of ServiceDeskFacade
  The facade is constructed by FastAPI dependency providers.
  If no TicketSubject is supplied, it creates one and attaches
  AuditLogObserver and EmailNotifierObserver.
end note
@enduml
